 "script": [
  "Wind and sun, which usually carry a large part of German power, nearly stopped around 12 December 2024: on average they supplied 2.1 GW, against 23.9 GW in the days before.",
  "Prices answered. The day-ahead price in Germany averaged €396/MWh on 12 December 2024 and reached €936/MWh at 16:00 UTC, against €126/MWh in the days before.",
  "The Germans call this a Dunkelflaute, a dark lull. The shortfall is met by gas, coal and imports, so the price follows the dearest plant that has to run.",
  "Our data shows the lull and the price. It does not show which plants filled the gap hour by hour in the neighbours, so we do not claim that."
 ],
